# What does flush_lines cost? Release build, -march=native, plugged in, 2026-09-19.
# Median of 1800 calls after 200 discarded; the two Clock::now() reads cost ~15 ns
# and are included in every row.

empty (two clock reads only)         15.0 ns
80 B: clflushopt only (no fence)     15.0 ns
80 B: + sfence                       17.0 ns
80 B: + sfence + mfence (as built)  422.0 ns
mfence alone                         27.0 ns

flush_lines cost vs region size (lines already clean: instruction cost only):
       80 B (    2 lines)     128.0 ns    64.00 ns/line
     4096 B (   64 lines)     260.0 ns     4.06 ns/line
    65536 B ( 1024 lines)    2672.0 ns     2.61 ns/line
   262144 B ( 4096 lines)   10370.0 ns     2.53 ns/line
  1048576 B (16384 lines)   19516.5 ns     1.19 ns/line

same, but every line dirtied first (what the runner actually flushes);
the dirtying pass is measured separately and subtracted:
       80 B (    2 lines)     294.0 ns   147.00 ns/line  (dirtying alone    16.0 ns)
     4096 B (   64 lines)    1135.0 ns    17.73 ns/line  (dirtying alone    25.0 ns)
    65536 B ( 1024 lines)   13227.5 ns    12.92 ns/line  (dirtying alone   939.0 ns)
   262144 B ( 4096 lines)   24277.0 ns     5.93 ns/line  (dirtying alone  3839.0 ns)
  1048576 B (16384 lines)   90375.5 ns     5.52 ns/line  (dirtying alone 15007.0 ns)
